# Environment for scripts/openrouter-smoketest/ ONLY.
#
# The scoring library in src/evalharness/ needs NO API key and makes no model calls.
# Nothing here is required to run the test suite.
#
# WARNING: do NOT `cp .env.example .env` if you already have a .env. That overwrites
# it. Append the lines you need instead.
#
# .env is gitignored at any depth, so it may live here at the repo root or in
# scripts/openrouter-smoketest/. The script searches both, script-local first.

# --- OpenRouter -------------------------------------------------------------------
# Get a key at https://openrouter.ai/keys
# Any ONE of these names works. The script accepts all three, checked in this order:
#   OPENROUTER_API_KEY, OPEN_ROUTER_API, OPENROUTER_KEY
OPENROUTER_API_KEY=

# --- Models ------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Verified against the live /models endpoint (338 models) on 2026-08-04, queried with
# a real key rather than scraped, because a summarised scrape of that list drops
# entries and produced a wrong answer once already.

# Incumbent: the exact model production runs today.
# Accepts audio input, so it can replicate production's one-call audio->JSON shape.
OPENROUTER_MODEL_INCUMBENT=google/gemini-2.5-flash

# Candidate: text/image/video only, NO audio. This is the whole migration problem in
# one line: production sends audio, the candidate cannot receive it, so a separate
# ASR step and a transcript artifact have to exist that do not exist today.
OPENROUTER_MODEL_CANDIDATE=qwen/qwen3.6-27b

# Second candidate. NOTE: "gemma-4-12b-it" does not exist on OpenRouter. Available
# Gemma 4 sizes are 26b-a4b and 31b; the only 12B is Gemma *3*. Pick deliberately:
#   google/gemma-3-12b-it       12B, gen 3, cheapest ($0.05/$0.15 per Mtok)
#   google/gemma-4-26b-a4b-it   gen 4, MoE  ($0.07/$0.34)
#   google/gemma-4-31b-it       gen 4, dense ($0.10/$0.34)
OPENROUTER_MODEL_CANDIDATE_2=google/gemma-4-26b-a4b-it

# --- True AI Token Factory ----------------------------------------------------------
# Internal endpoint, on-network only (see token-factory-probe.ps1 at the repo root).
# Placeholder only -- nothing under src/ reads this yet.
TOKEN_FACTORY_API_KEY=

# --- ASR ON OPENROUTER: 19 MODELS, 8 OPEN-WEIGHT -----------------------------------
# CORRECTED 2026-08-17. This block previously said "NOT AVAILABLE ON OPENROUTER", on the
# evidence that searching all 338 models for asr/speech/transcribe/whisper/audio returned
# exactly two, both OpenAI. That search was run correctly and the conclusion drawn from it
# was still wrong:
#
#   OpenRouter EXCLUDES speech-to-text models from GET /api/v1/models entirely.
#
# They are only visible under an explicit filter. Re-measured 2026-08-17:
#
#   curl "https://openrouter.ai/api/v1/models?output_modalities=transcription"   -> 19 models
#   curl "https://openrouter.ai/api/v1/models"                                   -> 0 of them
#
# qwen/qwen3-asr-flash-2026-02-10 -- named above as proof of absence -- is in fact served.
# So is qwen3-asr-1.7b, the same weights the internal GPU runs.
#
# Note the shape of the mistake, because the header of this file warns about its sibling
# ("a summarised scrape of that list drops entries and produced a wrong answer once
# already"). Here nothing was dropped by a summariser: the API itself does not return these
# rows without being asked. An absence proof needs the query that would have found the
# thing, not just a query that did not.
#
# The 8 open-weight ones, which are the only candidates that can be self-hosted:
#   openai/whisper-large-v3           Apache-2.0   Thai yes (99+ languages)
#   openai/whisper-large-v3-turbo     MIT          Thai yes (99+ languages)
#   qwen/qwen3-asr-1.7b               Apache-2.0   Thai yes (30 languages)
#   qwen/qwen3-asr-0.6b               Apache-2.0   Thai yes (30 languages)
#   mistralai/voxtral-small-24b-2507-stt  Apache-2.0   NO Thai
#   mistralai/voxtral-mini-3b-2507        Apache-2.0   NO Thai
#   nvidia/parakeet-tdt-0.6b-v3           CC-BY-4.0    NO Thai (European only)
#   nvidia/nemotron-3.5-asr-streaming-multilingual-0.6b  OpenMDW-1.1  Thai "adaptation-
#                                     ready" only -- needs fine-tuning, not a usable arm
#
# WHAT IS STILL TRUE: no THAI-SPECIALISED model is on OpenRouter. Typhoon
# (typhoon-ai/typhoon-whisper-large-v3, MIT) and Pathumma (nectec/, Apache-2.0) are
# HuggingFace-only, so the Thai-tuned candidates do still need the internal GPU. What
# changed is that the generic baselines and controls no longer do.
#
# Endpoint shape is NOT the chat one:
#   POST https://openrouter.ai/api/v1/audio/transcriptions
#   {"model": ..., "input_audio": {"data": "<base64 raw bytes>", "format": "wav"},
#    "language": "th"}
# asr-eval/scripts/transcribe.py --body-mode json speaks it.
